From 1fa78ecd176acf5a898eab799d0cbf44a1c9501e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwert-Xx <128706845+qwert-Xx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:29:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: imx50-epdc: expose owned WB direct-drive sessions

Reserve a synthetic waveform DMA table and derive A2 electrode actions
at startup. Drive fixed-color FULL updates on LUT0, count EOF progress
in IRQ context and restart completed LUTs in the owner worker. Exclude
normal updates while the session owns the panel.

Separate mmap inode references from device fd ownership and revoke
mappings before draining STOP. Restore full canvas history, including
SNAPSHOT capture, after STOP; stop on last fd close, suspend and removal.
Keep stopped core objects alive for outstanding device files.

Derive WB layout from buffer dimensions, roundup4 pitch and allocated
bytes. Register ioctl type 0xB8, commands 00-1F. WAIT_FRAME compares the
last returned frame/generation cursor against IRQ progress and returns
existing progress immediately, using only irq_lock.

Count EOF only while the session LUT is live and WB processing has
completed. Preserve cumulative progress across restarts and increase
generation for later submissions even when no frames were scanned.
Keep EOF-only interrupts off the normal-priority owner worker.
